# Pcap analysis

On Windows, dissect captures with:

`"c:\Program Files\Wireshark\tshark.exe"`

Do not write one-off Node/Python pcap parsers when tshark can decode the file.

This project writes classic pcap `LINKTYPE_LTALK` (114); frames start with LLAP. tshark protocols: `llap`, `ddp`, `nbp`, `atp`, `asp`, `afp`.

```text
tshark -r capture.pcap -T fields -e frame.number -e frame.time_relative -e llap.dst -e llap.src -e atp.function -e atp.tid -e asp.function -e afp.command
tshark -r capture.pcap -Y "atp || asp || afp" -V
tshark -r capture.pcap -q -z conv,atalk
```

Quote the tshark path in PowerShell. Prefer `-Y` display filters over dumping every frame.